+For a nonempty finite integer target S=R+R, translation by any fixed root element injects R into S, proving root finiteness. Diagonal extrema give minS=2minR and maxS=2maxR. Odd minimum is NO, including negative odd minima. For even t=minS, B=S-t and root translation by-t/2 give a bijective integer-root equivalence, including negative t. Put M=maxS-minS. Any normalized integer root has minimum0 and maximumM/2.
